With this change:

- Valid GeoJSON holes (clockwise) no longer trigger the split and are passed intact (with their `holes` array) to Earcut, which will correctly subtract them.
- Only mis‐oriented rings (holes that are CCW) will still be split out so that they get drawn as separate fills (as before), preserving backwards compatibility.
